    <!-- ECe and dS/m in a few words (heuristic evaluation, problem 6) -->
    <string name="ece_help_open">What ECe and dS/m mean</string>
    <string name="ece_help_title">What does ECe measure?</string>
    <string name="ece_help_what">ECe is the electrical conductivity of the soil, measured in its saturation extract: it tells how much salt the soil holds. Crop thresholds are set with this measure.</string>
    <string name="ece_help_unit">It is expressed in dS/m (decisiemens per meter). More dS/m means more salt.</string>
    <string name="ece_help_threshold">Each crop tolerates salt up to a threshold; table grape, for example, up to 1.5 dS/m. When the ECe goes above it, salt starts to lower the harvest.</string>
    <string name="ece_help_close">Got it</string>

